[1.8, "o", "\r\nBN-6  bug  in_stock refuses the last unit on hand\r\n\r\n  in_stock says no when a customer orders exactly the units left: with 2 on hand, an order for 2 is refused. Ordering up to the units on hand must be allowed; more than that is still refused.\r\n\r\ntriage  wrote .workflow/BN-6/triage.json\r\nbranch  BN-6-in-stock-refuses-the-last-unit (created from master, no origin remote)\r\nroute   light path: triage, change, commit, pr  (no plan up front; wb finish holds the change to the floor)\r\n        no plan, no other skill: make the change and a test that covers it, then\r\n        wb finish BN-6 -m \"<type>: <summary>\" --commit -- it runs the suite and every check,\r\n        commits exactly the checked files, and speaks only if something blocks\r\nBN-6  change todo  light path: make the change and a test that covers it\r\n  next: wb finish BN-6 -m \"<type>: <summary>\" --commit\r\n"]
